gui.wormholetech.tablet.p0.title=Fragment I — Discovery
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p0.l1=[Translation] Looks like some ancient civilization wrote this.
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p0.l2=[Translation] Technology that makes use of wormholes — not magic, but geometry folded thin.
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p0.l3=[Translation] Whatever can be automated, automate. The builders never worked by hand.


gui.wormholetech.tablet.p2.title=Fragment II — Matter
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p2.l1=[Translation] Matter path: craft the ore, place it, then blow it up.
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p2.l2=[Translation] Synthetic Ore + explosion -> Refined Naquadah (75%% per block). Mining just returns the ore.

gui.wormholetech.tablet.p3.title=Fragment III — Power
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p3.l1=[Translation] Power path — each step borrows more of the wormhole:
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p3.l2=[Translation] Naquadah Generator (%s RF/t for %s) -> Wormhole Energy Converter (%s RF/t, steady while a wormhole is open).

gui.wormholetech.tablet.p4.title=Fragment V — Echoes
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p4.l1=[Translation] An item is remembered across a throat of space. Making use of the rematerialization past the event horizon.
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p4.l2=[Translation] A wormhole stays open while a Block of Refined Naquadah decays (%s each). The Unstable Duplicator echoes only once, then collapses.

gui.wormholetech.tablet.p5.title=Fragment IV — Seeking Veins
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p5.l1=[Translation] Tells your machinery what veins to look for.
gui.wormholetech.tablet.p5.l2=[Translation] Requires Immersive Engineering Excavator to extract the minerals.

